# vertx5-mcp — HTTP request collection
# Works with: HTTPie Desktop · VS Code REST Client · JetBrains HTTP Client
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@agentBase    = http://localhost:8080
@mcpBase      = http://localhost:3001
@mcpSessionId = <replace-after-initialize>


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Health
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Health Check
GET {{agentBase}}/health


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Trade Failures
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 1) T-100 — Known deterministic (Missing ISIN)
POST {{agentBase}}/trade/failures
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tradeId": "T-100",
  "reason": "Missing ISIN"
}

### 2) T-200 — Unknown failure (agent classification)
POST {{agentBase}}/trade/failures
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tradeId": "T-200",
  "reason": "LEI not found in registry"
}

### 3) T-500 — Settlement amount mismatch · FX root-cause hypothesis (4 steps)
POST {{agentBase}}/trade/failures
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tradeId": "T-500",
  "reason": "Settlement amount mismatch detected"
}

### 4) T-600 — Duplicate trade detection · risk exposure analysis (4 steps)
POST {{agentBase}}/trade/failures
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tradeId": "T-600",
  "reason": "Possible duplicate trade execution"
}

### 5) T-700 — Regulatory T+1 deadline · compliance urgency (4 steps)
POST {{agentBase}}/trade/failures
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tradeId": "T-700",
  "reason": "Regulatory T+1 deadline at risk"
}

### 6) T-800 — Sanctions screening · adaptive false-positive analysis (5 steps)
POST {{agentBase}}/trade/failures
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tradeId": "T-800",
  "reason": "OFAC screening flag on counterparty"
}

### 7) T-900 — Multi-leg cascade · structural reasoning (5 steps)
POST {{agentBase}}/trade/failures
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tradeId": "T-900",
  "reason": "Linked trade cascade failure on swap leg"
}

### 8) T-1000 — Counterparty credit event · portfolio analysis (5 steps)
POST {{agentBase}}/trade/failures
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tradeId": "T-1000",
  "reason": "Counterparty credit downgrade to CCC+"
}


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  MCP — Streamable HTTP (2025-03-26)
#  Step 1: run "Initialize session" and copy Mcp-Session-Id from
#          the response header into @mcpSessionId above.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### MCP 1) Initialize session
POST {{mcpBase}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 1,
  "method": "initialize",
  "params": {
    "protocolVersion": "2025-03-26",
    "capabilities": {},
    "clientInfo": { "name": "http-client", "version": "1.0" }
  }
}

### MCP 2) List tools
POST {{mcpBase}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Mcp-Session-Id: {{mcpSessionId}}

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 2,
  "method": "tools/list"
}

### MCP 3) Invoke tool — case.raiseTicket
POST {{mcpBase}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Mcp-Session-Id: {{mcpSessionId}}

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 3,
  "method": "tools/call",
  "params": {
    "name": "case.raiseTicket",
    "arguments": {
      "tradeId": "T-300",
      "category": "ReferenceData",
      "summary": "MCP test"
    }
  }
}

### MCP 4) Ping
POST {{mcpBase}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Mcp-Session-Id: {{mcpSessionId}}

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 4,
  "method": "ping"
}

### MCP 5) Terminate session
DELETE {{mcpBase}}/mcp
Mcp-Session-Id: {{mcpSessionId}}


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  MCP — Legacy SSE (2024-11-05)
#  Step 1: open GET /sse in a browser or with --stream in HTTPie.
#          Copy the sessionId from the "endpoint" SSE event into
#          @mcpSessionId above, then run the POST below.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### MCP Legacy 1) Open SSE stream  (use HTTPie: http --stream GET {{mcpBase}}/sse)
GET {{mcpBase}}/sse

### MCP Legacy 2) tools/list via POST /message
POST {{mcpBase}}/message?sessionId={{mcpSessionId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 1,
  "method": "tools/list"
}
